            <ArticleTitle>[Abdominopelvic actinomycosis in pseudo-tumoral form: diagnosis by ultrasonography-guided biopsy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>364-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a case of abdominopelvic actinomycosis, a rare bacterial infection. This case is exceptional for its clinical tumoral expression with fistulization through the skin, and for its rapid diagnosis by ultrasonically-guided needle biopsy. The clinical, bacteriological, histological and therapeutic aspects of actinomycosis are detailed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
